<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17745" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fascĭno</span></b> , āre,
			v. a.
		cf. Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάσκανος, βασκαίνω</span>, v.
			fascinum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to enchant</i>, <i>bewitch</i>, <i>charm</i>, <i>fascinate</i> by the
			eyes or the tongue: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nescio quis teneros oculus mihi fascinat agnos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 3, 103</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">malā linguā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat. 7,
					12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">contra fascinantes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					13, 4, 9, § 40</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animal fascinatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. Vet. 7, 73</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vos non obedire veritati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Galat. 3, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
